      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1og3daa'
    '|a||So if we count gains and losses, what does the counting look like?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Kahneman and Tversky drew it as a curve. Across, the change in money: gains to the right, losses to the left. Up, how it feels.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:138fgdi'
    '|b||Gains first. The first hundred dollars feels great, the tenth hundred adds less, so the curve bends over.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:zy0dk7'
    '|b||Losses mirror that, but steeper. In their words, losses loom larger than gains.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:e2cff3'
    '|a||How much steeper?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1y8wwvc'
    '|b||In their 1992 follow-up, a loss weighed about two and a quarter times an equal gain. That ratio is loss aversion. Call it lambda.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:s87bem'
    '|a||So offer me a coin flip: lose five hundred dollars or win seven hundred and fifty. On average I come out ahead.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1qbm0eh'
    '|b||But on this curve the lost five hundred hurts more than the seven fifty pleases. So you say no, as most people do when offered bets like this.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:111j4n2'
    '|b||The bends lean you, too. Bent over among gains, you prefer a sure thing; bent the other way among losses, you''d gamble to dodge a sure loss.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:fgo1a7'
    '|a||Try it: slide lambda down toward one, where a loss weighs no more than a gain, and watch the refusal turn into a yes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:s8g6xw'
    '|a||Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||In symbols, the curve is a power of the gain on the right, and lambda times a power of the loss on the left.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||With their estimates, alpha about 0.88 and lambda about 2.25.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:pkr2f'
    '|a||So you turn down the flip whenever lambda is above about 1.4.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:6tsm8o'
    '|a||So the curve has two features: a kink at the reference point, and a bend on each side of it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1qp0kmi'
    '|b||That curve has its zero at the reference point. But who decides where the zero sits?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||In the puzzle, the question did. ''You''ve been given a thousand'' puts the zero at a thousand.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10bltgd'
    '|b||Then both options are gains: fifteen hundred for sure, or a flip between a thousand and two thousand. On the bent-over side, the sure thing wins.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:4f4r84'
    '|a||Now: ''You''ve been given two thousand.'' Slide the zero there, and the same options become losses: five hundred down for sure, or a flip between a thousand down and nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ski6dw'
    '|a||Now the zero sits at 2,000. Which does the curve pick? Tap it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1v0a3la'
    '|a||Now the zero sits at 2,000. Which does the curve pick?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The coin flip: yes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Among losses the curve bends the other way, so the flip hurts less than the sure loss. The gamble wins, as it did for sixty-nine percent of the respondents.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Same money, same curve. Only the zero moved.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:41awjx'
    '|b||And outside the lab, the zero is usually what you already have, or what you expected to get.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1mhf8ff'
    '|a||Your turn: slide the reference point and lambda, and find where the choice flips.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:j69txq'
    '|a||With lambda at one it flips at fifteen hundred. The more loss-averse the curve, the further the zero has to move before it gambles.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So which side of the kink you stand on, and which way you lean, is decided by the zero, not by the final amount.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1whghgw'
    '|b||So is two to one a law of nature?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||The evidence for some kink is real. Professional golfers sink putts for par about two percentage points more often than putts for birdie from the same distance.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:lbkgb9'
    '|a||Par is their reference point, and a missed par feels like a loss.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:2nu23i'
    '|a||And a 2024 meta-analysis, pooling hundreds of estimates, put average loss aversion at about two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ti27yw'
    '|b||But a second 2024 meta-analysis, of risky choices only, found about 1.3. And with small stakes, Eyal Ert and Ido Erev found people close to neutral.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1tor431'
    '|b||In 2018, David Gal and Derek Rucker went further: the evidence, they argued, doesn''t show that losses generally loom larger at all.':
      mp3: 
